APEX ACADEMIC UNIVERSITY
Student Attendance Policy and Absence Regulations
DOCUMENT TITLE: Student Attendance Policy and Absence Regulations
DOCUMENT TYPE: attendance_policy
EFFECTIVE DATE: Fall Semester 2025 | VERSION: 3.0
SECTION 1: MANDATORY ATTENDANCE REQUIREMENTS
1.1 Students enrolled in undergraduate and postgraduate programs are expected to attend all scheduled lectures, tutorials,
laboratory sessions, and seminars.
1.2 A minimum cumulative attendance of 75% across all registered courses in a semester is strictly mandatory to maintain
academic eligibility.
1.3 Students falling between 65% and 74% attendance due to documented medical conditions or institutional representation
must submit a formal condonation request to the Academic Dean within 5 working days of the absence.
SECTION 2: ABSENCE LIMITS AND COURSE WITHDRAWAL
2.1 If a student exceeds 6 consecutive unexcused absences in a single course, the Course Instructor is required to submit
an Academic Advisory Warning to the Registrar.
2.2 If a student's total attendance in a course drops below 60%, the student is automatically withdrawn from the course with
a grade of 'W/F' (Withdrawn/Failed) and is ineligible to sit for the End-Semester Examination for that course.
2.3 Maximum allowable medical leave in a single semester is 14 calendar days, subject to verified medical certification from
an empaneled university physician.
SECTION 3: APPEALS AND CONDONATION PROCEDURE
3.1 Condonation for attendance shortage up to 10% may be granted by the Academic Dean upon payment of a condonation
fee of $50 per course and submission of valid medical documentation.
3.2 No condonation is permitted under any circumstances if attendance drops below 65%.
3.3 Attendance records are updated weekly on the University Student Portal. Appeals regarding attendance discrepancies
must be filed within 7 days of the portal update.